  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Ensure that any failure in doCommit() logs an error message, not a warning - specifically any failure due to failing to update the objectStore, datastreamStore, registry, fieldSearch or resourceIndex should be logged as an error.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Tidy up the ingest recovery vs purge code.  Currently the purge code is re-used as ingest tidy-up to remove any artefacts that were committed due to a failed ingest.  These are separate concerns.  Specifically failures on purge should be logged as errors; whereas failure to remove a failed ingest artefact could be a warning due to an ingest failing part-way through.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
