      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Logging tidied up to report updates to storage, index etc as errors (and also include pid in messages).</p>\n\n<p>Object removal code moved to separate method, with a \"failSafe\" parameter; true indicates warn only, false indicates we were doing a purge and therefore any error removing artefacts is an error condition.</p>\n\n<p>We could in future change behaviour to throw an exception if a purge fails; or would it be better to report the error and continue (since the repository can still be used; albeit with potential inconsistences in the storage).</p>",
     "created": "05/Mar/12 11:16 AM",
     "id": "12256",
     "jsdPublic": true,
